<title>BELGIUM: France has not sought to reopen EMU stability pact.</title>
<headline>France has not sought to reopen EMU stability pact.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>France has not officially requested any reopening of the stability pact for economic and monetary union, a Dutch EU presidency spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no official demand from (French finance) minister Dominique Strauss-Kahn whatsoever,&quot; the spokesman said.  </p>
<p>The spokesman was speaking ahead of a meeting on Sunday and Monday of EU finance ministers, the first to be attended by Strauss-Kahn.</p>
<p>During the French election campaign socialist candidates said they wanted to reopen discussion of the stability pact. A number of EU officials have been playing down the statements as campaign rhetoric.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
